Description: Keel overlay: Anubis, proof of work behind Nginx
 The Anubis overlay of Keel Linux (handbook decisions 0030 and 0036):
 Anubis, built by Keel, run as the instance anubis@keel.service on the
 IPv6 loopback, and the overlay manifest keel reads, installed as
 /usr/share/keel/overlays/anubis.yaml (decision 0041).
 .
 The instance is installed disabled and stopped, the state of a simple
 installation; keel spec apply enables and starts it where the instance
 spec says so. Its signing key is made on the machine at the first start,
 when it is not there, and never ships in an image. Nginx sends a location
 through Anubis with /etc/nginx/snippets/keel-anubis.conf.
